Process

    1. Why IT struggles
        1.1 There are different roles with different responsibilities and focus.
        1.2 All of these roles come together to create the product which the client hopefully needs and will pay for.
        1.3 When both the team, company and the product is small it is easy to align and communicate with each other.
        1.4 As the company grows larger, different roles and teams may not be in sync and then stop communicating altogether because of the problems.
        1.5 This is where the devops mindset and culture comes in to provide a structure, framework and reality for people on the company to understand 
        that they together make or break the product, value the company is shipping.
    2. The birth and evolution of devops
        2.1 In 2009 john allspaw and paul hammond  presentation. Later patrick debois put together the devops days.
        2.2 The pheonix project
        2.3 How can we deliver better, faster and more compliant software.
        2.4 DevOps handbook
        2.5 The unicorn project
        2.6 Agile/lean
        2.7 Effective devops book
        2.8 DevOps adoption book
        2.9 Define and standardize processes, later find ways to automate them so that everything is integrated like a factory line. I think, this is the soul of devops.
